# NOT `std.file_system` -- that module is a MOCK ("Mock implementations for
# pure Simple demonstration"): its `file_write_text` writes nothing and returns
# `true`, and its `file_read_text` consults `file_exists_mock`. Binding the
# capsule-receipt writer to it produced a receipt that was never on disk while
# reporting success, surfacing later as `native-capsule-receipt-invalid`.
# `file_write_exact`/`file_read_nullable` are uniquely named and rt-backed, so
# they cannot be captured by the same-arity `file_write_text` overload set.
